{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Replace six verbs with one noun and a coherent verb set.\n\n    rebar bridge setup | doctor/fsck | status | preview | sync | pause | resume\n\nThree verbs retire. `reconcile` goes with NO alias, because the defaults invert: `rebar reconcile`\nwith no arguments means dry-run (the CLI wrapper injects `--mode dry-run` at\n`_cli/__init__.py:145-160`, while `python -m rebar_reconciler` itself defaults to LIVE, and\n`_lib_ops.py:92` defaults to dry-run again — three entry points, two conventions). `bridge sync`\nwith no arguments mutates. Aliasing would be a silent behaviour change; anyone with `reconcile` in\na script must re-read the line.\n\n`bridge-status` retires because its producer has never existed in this repo — rebar was extracted\nfrom digital-service-orchestra on 2026-06-08 and the reader was a knowing tombstone from day one.\nNote the citation in its docstring, \"epic 3a03\", is DANGLING: in this repo 3a03 resolves to an\nunrelated test-isolation bug created 11 days AFTER the comment citing it. The real epic is\n`3006-e198-13db-4e1f`.\n\n`purge-bridge` retires: five commits, every one an automated lint sweep or safety retrofit, none a\nfeature or bug fix, and no script, workflow, or runbook invokes it. Its `--keep` flag is also\ninverted-sense (it deletes everything NOT matching).\n\n`--mode` disappears entirely. Its five values collapse to `preview`/`sync` plus `--max-changes N`;\nthe two `bootstrap-*` values carry no semantics beyond their cap integer (the only non-applier\nconsumers test `MODE_CAPS[m] != 0` and never read 10 or 100).\n\nFlags survive only if their help text can be written without internals. Ten candidates reduced to\nthree: `--max-changes N`, `--only <ids>`, `--except <ids>`, `--max-age <duration>`, plus the house\n`--output json`. Maintainer decision: `--only`/`--except` limit what is EXAMINED as well as what is\nchanged (unlike the internal `--filter-local-ids` they replace, which filtered only writes and was\nmarked \"for validation use only\" for that reason), and preview/sync remains the read/write knob.\n\n`check-access` is its own verb, not a flag on the health verb: all three narrowing-flag precedents\n(`flux check --pre`, `dbt debug --connection`, `gh auth status`) are READ-ONLY, and none mutates the\nremote — so the precedent does not transfer to an operation that creates and deletes a real Jira\nissue. `fsck` audits your records; `check-access` proves your access.\n\n`setup` calls `check-access` as its final validation step.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar bridge <verb>` exists with the agreed verb set\n- [ ] `reconcile`, `bridge-status`, `purge-bridge` are removed, with release notes; no aliases\n- [ ] `--mode` is gone from the CLI and the engine entrypoint (`_cli/__init__.py:145-160`,\n      `rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:501-508`, `mode.py`)\n- [ ] **Surface scope is explicit (review remediation).** `reconcile`/`mode` lives on THREE surfaces,\n      not one: the CLI, the public library API `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)` (`src/rebar/__init__.py:51`\n      re-exporting `_lib_ops.py:92`), and the MCP tool `reconcile(mode=...)` (`_mcp_reads.py:279`,\n      surfaced via `mcp_server.py`). THIS ticket retires the CLI + engine only. The library and MCP\n      retirements belong to sibling `f789`, which ADDS the bridge surface to those same two\n      interfaces — so each surface's old verb is removed by the same change that ships its\n      replacement, leaving no window where an MCP or library caller has neither. `f789` already\n      depends_on this ticket, which enforces that order.\n- [ ] A test asserts the CLI no longer accepts `--mode` or the `reconcile` verb, AND that the library\n      and MCP entrypoints are still callable at this ticket's boundary (proving the staged retirement\n      left no surface broken mid-epic)\n- [ ] Every shipped flag's help text contains no internals (no \"mode\", \"rank\", \"gate\", \"lock\", \"cap\", \"pass\", \"binding store\", no exit-code numbers)\n- [ ] `bridge` appears in `rebar --help`; today `reconcile` appears ZERO times while three bridge verbs (one dead) are listed\n- [ ] The dangling \"epic 3a03\" citation is corrected wherever it survives"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786084672008358001,"uuid":"3390936d-c381-4a6e-9b2c-b645d3730b8a"}